    "long_instructions": "## **Do This:**\r\n\r\n1. This code paints a path partway to the cone. Run it to see where it stops.\r\n2. Add `move()`, `turn_left()`, and `paint(\"white\")` commands to keep painting until the painter reaches the traffic cone.",
    "start_sources": {
      "files": {
        "0": {
          "id": "0",
          "name": "main.py",
          "contents": "# Set up painter commands\nfrom neighborhood import *\n\n# Sets the amount of paint for the painter\nset_paint(14)\n\n# The painter starts top left corner, facing the food truck\npaint(\"white\")\nmove()\npaint(\"white\")\nmove()\npaint(\"white\")\nturn_left()\nturn_left()\nturn_left()\nmove()\npaint(\"white\")\nmove()\npaint(\"white\")\nturn_left()\nmove()\npaint(\"white\")\nmove()\npaint(\"white\")\n# Add your code below",
